  "safety": [
    "Do not mix chemistries, brands or charge states in one device.",
    "Only NiMH and USB-rechargeable lithium-ion AAA batteries are designed to be recharged; charging alkaline, zinc-carbon or lithium iron disulfide AAA batteries can cause leakage or rupture."
  ],
  "notes": "JIS UM-4 names the zinc-carbon battery and AM-4 the alkaline battery. Wikipedia also lists ZR03 for nickel oxyhydroxide; no datasheet was found for that battery.",
